WEBVTT

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:27.540
Damn it, one of our own got attacked!
They expect us to sit on our asses?

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:29.620
This is ridiculous!

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:32.880
Even so, orders are orders.

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:35.960
I don't agree, either, but what can we do?

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:37.510
Hey, what's the matter?

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:38.940
We just got orders to stand by.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:40.000
From Eric?

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.100
Apparently, the security footage
of the attack was erased.

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.560
So someone's on the inside?

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:51.320
We've been instructed
not to act too boldly right now.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:52.280
Most likely-

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:54.610
What, they don't trust us?

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.950
Calm down. It's the opposite.

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:02.070
It's as Boris says.
Right now, it's wise to stay quiet.

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:03.540
Boris!

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:08.710
These were outside the station house.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:30.060
How did it go?

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:34.530
We still have to be cautious,
but he seems to be out of danger.

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:36.980
There shouldn't be any permanent damage.

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:38.570
Any defensive wounds?

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:40.650
I didn't see any.

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:42.830
The natural assumption would be

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:45.580
someone standing next to him
suddenly attacked him.

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:49.660
Of course, I'm no expert,
so that's entirely speculation.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:57.580
You're with the RIS, then?

00:01:57.580 --> 00:02:01.180
I hate to trouble you with formalities,
but can you sign here?

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:02.550
Oh. Sure.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.520
Excuse me, Mr. Flick?

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:18.520
Before he lost consciousness,
he begged me to do something.

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:22.450
He insisted that I give this
to one Keith Flick.

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:50.180
Any risk of permanent damage?

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:52.560
Essentially zero, they said.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:55.850
His wound might ache on cold days,
that sort of thing.

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:58.190
The doctor said it was a miracle.

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:04.280
Understood.
I'll send some people over to stand guard.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:08.120
Once they arrive, the rest of you
come back to work on the case.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:09.120
But we...

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:13.880
I'll send Brody and Takeda.
That's better than you and Keith, right?

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:16.580
Okay, that's a relief.

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:18.400
Lily.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:18.920
Yes?

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:21.260
Keep Bran's condition under wraps.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:23.130
He might be attacked again.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:27.380
For now, we can't trust anyone
outside the RIS.

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:28.310
Yes, sir.

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:56.040
How's that?

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:00.340
It's better than before! There's no buzz,
and it's sustaining again!

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.250
What was causing it?

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:05.090
It wasn't just one thing.
Take a look right here.

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:06.590
See? Right here.

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:09.350
A youngster wouldn't understand.

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:11.360
You're a true craftsman!

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:12.850
Aren't I? Keep up the praise!

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:13.770
He's here!

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:15.850
Look, that's him!
Touch Canopus.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:29.530
Canopus.

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:40.000
Keith!

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:44.670
You've been acting weird
ever since the hospital!

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:48.380
Why'd you stop all of a sudden?

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:51.220
I need to stop at that market.

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:52.800
What?

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:55.350
Hang on, you're shopping?

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:57.420
I need to use their bathroom.

00:04:57.420 --> 00:04:58.350
Again?

00:04:58.640 --> 00:04:59.610
Number two.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:02.070
You're definitely lying.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:04.020
Come in with me, then.

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:07.240
I can't-- Hey! Come back here!

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.440
Stupid Genie!

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:23.960
This is gonna be tough.

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:28.630
Yeah?

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:29.630
Find anything?

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:33.840
All I can tell is that it's a mess,
both inside and out.

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:36.810
And given what's on it,
I can't request support.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:38.270
This will take time.

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:39.270
I see.

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:41.810
Call me if you find anything.

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:43.730
Oh, hang on, Eric.

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:47.110
Don't worry. He's out of danger.

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:50.530
Thank goodness.

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:51.570
Kaela.

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:53.280
"Keep it to myself," right?

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:54.200
Please do.

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:55.250
Roger that.

00:05:57.620 --> 00:05:59.750
Okay, Brandy,

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:01.790
what did you find?

00:06:13.050 --> 00:06:13.970
Yeah?

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:17.510
Kaela, it's me.
Switch us over to a secure line, okay?

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:19.060
Sure, one second.

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:21.230
Okay, go.

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:22.270
Are you busy?

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:25.150
-This had better be important--
-Whenever you're free.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:27.570
Send the following names to my cell.

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:30.480
It's sent, Keith.

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:32.530
Got it. Thanks.

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:36.450
-What do you need those for?
-I don't know yet.

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:38.040
That'll be a trillion yen.

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:39.200
For what?

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:45.090
Look, sir, I'm not running a charity here.
Bye now.

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:48.710
Damn it, I'm too busy for this.

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:08.600
I don't believe
you only used the bathroom.

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:11.730
You're reading too much into it.

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:16.200
Shut up! Shut your hole! This stinks!

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:19.200
Stinks, stinks, stinks!
And not just your poop!

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:20.830
It stinks, stinks, stinks!

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:40.510
That incontinent old fart's always trying
to leave me out of the loop.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:44.020
What? What?

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:46.480
Don't move. Put your hands up.

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:47.800
What are you doing?

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:48.840
Hands up!

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:52.900
Hand over your cell phone.

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:58.660
Yes, sir. Understood.

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:01.280
I'll deal with it at once.

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:03.120
What is it?

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.580
Apparently, he's still alive.

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:08.290
He'll be dead soon enough, right?

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:10.760
I can take care of it.

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:17.220
We can't afford to leave any trace behind.
Have our man inside kill him.

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:21.430
But he already botched the job once!
Is it smart to leave it to him?

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:23.730
After all, he's just an ordinary human.

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:25.220
Observe, but no more.

00:08:25.510 --> 00:08:28.980
If it looks like he'll fail again,
you may eliminate him.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:31.230
There are many who can replace him.

00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:32.400
Understood.

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:41.040
Hey, Minatsuki.
I'm already out of gold ampules.

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:43.250
Gimme!

00:08:43.780 --> 00:08:45.830
I hope you're not wasting them.

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:56.430
Hey, who do you think you're talking to,
you useless bitch?

00:08:58.230 --> 00:08:58.680
Kamui.

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:07.020
Use them more sparingly.

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:21.200
The time between Kamui's ampule doses
is getting shorter.

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:23.410
Yuna.

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:25.240
I didn't do anything.

00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:26.870
I know that.

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:30.340
Just in case things don't work out,
delete that program.

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:33.550
Huh? Are you sure?
It'll make things harder.

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:36.420
I'll think of something else.

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:39.260
That's an order. Yuna, do it right away.

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:40.630
All right.

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:43.510
Laica.

00:09:46.550 --> 00:09:48.140
Keep an eye on Kamui.

00:09:49.930 --> 00:09:53.820
I've got a pretty good idea now
of why somebody wanted Bran dead.

00:09:57.820 --> 00:09:59.070
Isn't that--

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:02.030
It's Bran's.
It had been dumped outside, apparently.

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:07.700
I was asked to try
to reconstruct the data on it.

00:10:07.950 --> 00:10:11.040
I did, but only fragments.

00:10:11.990 --> 00:10:13.580
And this is the result.

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:20.930
What do you want for lunch?

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:23.130
-Who's that?
-How about sushi?

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:24.600
Hey, good idea!

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:26.430
Is this our precinct?

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:29.720
Yep. Those two people are both
in Security Division.

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:31.100
Oh, you're right!

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:32.080
And now...

00:10:42.230 --> 00:10:44.910
The way it's hidden is really clever.

00:10:45.610 --> 00:10:49.370
It's a mystery
how Bran managed to discover it.

00:10:49.990 --> 00:10:54.250
What's certain is that without help
from someone inside the precinct,

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:57.250
operating this program would be difficult.

00:11:08.090 --> 00:11:10.890
Wait, are you saying--
These are tapped video feeds?

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:15.180
Bingo. It can jack into personal terminals
issued to station personnel at will,

00:11:15.180 --> 00:11:19.280
as well as every camera and audio source
inside the station house.

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:21.490
Even if they're turned off.

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:23.660
Its range seems to be limited, though.

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:24.700
No way.

00:11:25.190 --> 00:11:26.700
Creepy, huh?

00:11:27.070 --> 00:11:30.530
I've heard rumors
that programs like this existed.

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:34.620
In my crowd,
it's joked about as an urban legend.

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:39.670
-But that's the only thing it could be.
-Can you tell who put it there?

00:11:40.330 --> 00:11:43.640
It's unlikely we'll figure that out
from this.

00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:48.310
Kaela. Let's go to Keith with this.

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:51.760
Keith? That reminds me,
he called me a moment ago.

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:56.690
He asked me to send him a list of everyone
involved with the RIS the last five years.

00:11:57.100 --> 00:11:58.270
A personnel list?

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:01.070
What?

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:07.740
Damn it. It's gone.

00:12:08.110 --> 00:12:10.370
They got the drop on us. Let's go.

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:11.530
Go where?

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:12.960
To find Keith.

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:15.370
I'm almost certain he's onto something.

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:34.350
Things are already this bad,
and you just got back.

00:12:37.470 --> 00:12:39.520
Will your man pull through?

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:43.270
This is even worse than last time.

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:47.940
Back in college,
I often thought about something.

00:12:47.940 --> 00:12:52.280
I wondered if I could develop a medicine
to cure your bad attitude.

00:12:53.110 --> 00:12:58.250
I doubt it. For starters,
human beings weren't designed by humans.

00:12:58.740 --> 00:13:02.710
Up here in particular isn't designed
to be tampered with by people.

00:13:03.460 --> 00:13:06.880
I'll file a complaint
with the lead designer, then.

00:13:06.880 --> 00:13:08.170
Who do I talk to?

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:11.260
I guess that would be God.

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:17.640
Whenever I talk to you,
I get the worst craving for a cigarette.

00:13:19.640 --> 00:13:23.110
Gil, have you ever read Moby Dick?

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:27.990
That book by Melville?
You lent me a copy, remember?

00:13:28.730 --> 00:13:29.660
I read it.

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:34.500
In his last moments, I wonder
what was going through Ahab's mind

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:36.920
as he was going down with Moby Dick.

00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:39.580
Genie?

00:13:40.950 --> 00:13:44.050
It's no big deal.
Sorry, forget I said anything.

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:47.680
Well, I'm off to catch our criminal.

00:14:23.850 --> 00:14:24.550
Damn.

00:14:32.960 --> 00:14:37.970
This ain't someplace some big-band wannabe
should be wandering around.

00:14:37.970 --> 00:14:41.150
How about you hand over your wallet
and get lost.

00:14:41.470 --> 00:14:42.350
Shut up.

00:14:45.850 --> 00:14:47.150
Hey, now!

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:49.320
Move.

00:14:50.060 --> 00:14:52.070
You got a death wish, pal?

00:15:34.900 --> 00:15:36.700
Hey, what happened in here?

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:39.700
Hands in the air and don't move!

00:15:40.450 --> 00:15:41.620
Hey! Are you deaf?

00:15:49.080 --> 00:15:50.630
I'll leave you to clean up.

00:16:00.800 --> 00:16:01.680
Where did...

00:16:02.760 --> 00:16:04.680
Just stepped out.

00:16:12.520 --> 00:16:14.030
Hey, have you seen Keith?

00:16:15.150 --> 00:16:16.380
This again?

00:16:16.380 --> 00:16:17.450
What again?

00:16:18.150 --> 00:16:22.160
He came in a while ago.
But then he turned around and left again.

00:16:22.950 --> 00:16:23.830
Oh.

00:16:26.450 --> 00:16:27.330
Lily.

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:32.130
Since you're here, would you mind
making a delivery to Takeda and Brody?

00:16:32.710 --> 00:16:35.220
They asked me, but I forgot.

00:17:24.970 --> 00:17:27.560
Isn't that my knife?

00:17:28.470 --> 00:17:30.850
You stole it when you came over
for drinks.

00:17:32.890 --> 00:17:34.480
JHR.

00:17:35.600 --> 00:17:39.160
I got this from Brandon.
It was meant for me, for some reason.

00:17:40.440 --> 00:17:43.860
It's a vintage French model,
hacked, with its knob removed.

00:17:43.860 --> 00:17:45.160
The hands read 10:08.

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:47.830
The GMT bezel shows 18.

00:17:48.410 --> 00:17:52.630
GMT. Greenwich Mean Time.
English Standard Time.

00:17:53.790 --> 00:17:56.420
Ten, eight, 18.

00:17:57.500 --> 00:18:01.380
Converting the hands into letters
starting from the top, we get...

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:02.590
J, H, R.

00:18:03.590 --> 00:18:05.010
And French.

00:18:06.300 --> 00:18:07.510
It's a simple code.

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:10.100
The question is, why would Brandon

00:18:10.100 --> 00:18:13.650
resort to something so convoluted
when his life was in danger?

00:18:14.310 --> 00:18:16.690
He couldn't leave a message there.

00:18:17.230 --> 00:18:21.610
Because his attacker was able to return
to the scene and remove any evidence.

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:23.360
So, he started thinking.

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:27.320
As his consciousness was fading,
fearing he was going to die,

00:18:27.320 --> 00:18:30.120
he frantically thought
of how to get me a message.

00:18:31.160 --> 00:18:33.500
Five people at the precinct
have these initials.

00:18:33.790 --> 00:18:36.840
However, only one is called
by the French pronunciation.

00:18:37.580 --> 00:18:40.800
As a sign of trust and respect
from his fellow detectives.

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:45.270
I didn't want to believe it,
"Jean Henri Richard."

00:18:49.720 --> 00:18:50.730
It's you, right?

00:18:54.060 --> 00:18:54.940
Jean.

00:18:58.020 --> 00:18:59.150
Keith.

00:19:01.440 --> 00:19:02.990
How long have you known?

00:19:03.400 --> 00:19:07.410
I first suspected you eight years ago.
Right after that case.

00:19:07.820 --> 00:19:10.450
That's when I found
the multi-camera program.

00:19:10.700 --> 00:19:14.920
I'm surprised. You were pretending
to be my friend all that time?

00:19:15.830 --> 00:19:17.090
Look who's talking.

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:20.300
Keith Flick.

00:19:21.500 --> 00:19:24.050
I will never forgive you.

00:19:25.960 --> 00:19:28.470
I'll do it again and again.

00:19:29.590 --> 00:19:30.510
Jean?

00:19:30.510 --> 00:19:34.770
The people you care about
will die around you one by one.

00:19:36.310 --> 00:19:38.230
Just like back then,

00:19:38.520 --> 00:19:41.690
I'm going to take away
those closest to you again.

00:19:42.520 --> 00:19:44.780
I'll take them from you, completely.

00:19:45.650 --> 00:19:49.370
Will you be able to keep them safe
this time? I'm not so sure.

00:19:50.450 --> 00:19:51.370
Can you?

00:19:59.290 --> 00:20:00.960
You will be the last to go.

00:20:01.540 --> 00:20:03.180
Watch with those hateful eyes

00:20:03.710 --> 00:20:06.680
as everything falls to ruin around you.

00:20:10.010 --> 00:20:11.350
Keith Flick!

00:20:13.930 --> 00:20:16.020
Don't! Jean, put that down!

00:20:16.560 --> 00:20:21.610
Those you love most will be covered
in crimson.

00:20:22.690 --> 00:20:27.870
Like the cycle of death and rebirth,
it will repeat itself, continuing forever.

00:20:28.440 --> 00:20:31.410
An indelible code will be etched into you.

00:20:35.030 --> 00:20:37.290
I was murdered by you.

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:40.710
I'll see you in hell.

00:20:41.370 --> 00:20:42.420
Jean!

00:21:04.310 --> 00:21:05.150
Jean.

00:21:42.020 --> 00:21:42.900
Jean!

00:21:43.690 --> 00:21:46.240
Somebody! Anybody! Come here, hurry!

00:21:48.110 --> 00:21:52.440
I have a code seven! Officer stabbed
and badly injured at Royal Hospital!

00:21:52.440 --> 00:21:53.410
Attacker at large!

00:21:53.820 --> 00:21:55.860
Keith.
Likely still in the area!

00:21:55.860 --> 00:21:57.240
Requesting immediate dispatch!

00:21:57.240 --> 00:21:57.990
Run.

00:21:59.160 --> 00:21:59.960
Jean!

00:22:00.450 --> 00:22:02.450
Keith.
Don't die, Jean! Hang on!

00:22:02.450 --> 00:22:03.830
Hey, look at me!

00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:08.880
Jean.

00:22:29.110 --> 00:22:30.530
Are you Canopus?

00:22:35.570 --> 00:22:36.450
Hey.

00:22:39.070 --> 00:22:40.880
We meet at last,

00:22:42.700 --> 00:22:44.420
Killer B.

00:22:57.560 --> 00:23:03.520
Someday I’ll be gone

00:23:05.440 --> 00:23:12.110
To somewhere that we belong

00:23:13.490 --> 00:23:17.490
And god has never played his role

00:23:17.490 --> 00:23:20.790
Because I’m the one who saves my soul

00:23:20.790 --> 00:23:21.790
Or rather, 13.
